# Trivy suppressions for the tag-publish vulnerability gate (docker-ci.yml).
#
# Policy (#220): only CRITICAL/HIGH CVEs with NO fixed Debian 12 package may
# be listed here. Each entry names the affected package(s); prune entries as
# Debian ships fixes — Renovate base-image digest bumps re-run the scan and
# will fail if an entry stops matching a fixed package. Never list a CVE that
# has a fixed version available; fix the image instead.
#
# Every entry carries `exp:2026-11-02` (30-day time box): after that date the
# entry stops applying and must be re-verified and renewed or removed.
#
# Last re-verified 2026-10-03: both images (backend/Dockerfile on
# python:3.14-slim-bookworm, frontend/Dockerfile on node:24.21.0-bookworm-slim,
# current pinned digests) built locally and scanned with trivy 0.75.0
# (CRITICAL,HIGH, no ignore file). Every CVE below was reported with an empty
# FixedVersion (Debian status affected / fix_deferred / will_not_fix), i.e. no
# fixed bookworm package exists. Upstream tracking for each entry:
# https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/<CVE-ID>.
#
# Runtime context for the exploitability notes: the containers run only the
# podex Python app (backend) or `node` serving the Astro SSR build (frontend).
# Neither invokes perl, gzip, mount/nsenter/util-linux tools, systemd, or
# ncurses programs, and neither runs as a privileged/login environment.

# zlib1g — integer overflow in minizip zipOpenNewFileInZip4_64 (Debian:
# will_not_fix). minizip (contrib) is not used by Python/Node zlib bindings;
# unreachable.
CVE-2023-45853 exp:2026-11-02

# libsqlite3-0 (backend) — SQLite integer overflow (Debian: affected). Python's
# sqlite3 module is only used when DATABASE_URL is sqlite (local default);
# podex never executes attacker-supplied SQL, so the overflow trigger is not
# reachable.
CVE-2025-7458 exp:2026-11-02

# perl-base — perl core regex/pack issues and Archive-Tar / IO-Compress /
# Storable bugs (Debian: affected / fix_deferred). perl-base is an essential
# dpkg dependency in bookworm and cannot be removed from slim images; the app
# never runs perl, so none of these are reachable.
CVE-2026-8376 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-13221 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-42496 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-42497 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-48962 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-57432 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-57433 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-9538 exp:2026-11-02

# ncurses (ncurses-base/ncurses-bin/libtinfo6/libncursesw6) — buffer overflow
# (Debian: affected). No terminal UI runs in the containers; unreachable.
CVE-2025-69720 exp:2026-11-02

# gzip — LZH decompression buffer overflow (Debian: fix_deferred). The app
# never invokes the gzip binary on untrusted input; unreachable.
CVE-2026-41992 exp:2026-11-02

# libacl1 — symlink traversal via libacl functions (Debian: fix_deferred).
# Exploitation needs a privileged process manipulating ACLs on
# attacker-controlled paths; the app does not use ACL APIs.
CVE-2026-54369 exp:2026-11-02

# libpcre2-8-0 — out-of-bounds write via crafted regex (Debian: affected).
# Python `re` and V8 irregexp do not use PCRE2; only base-image CLI tools link
# it and they are never fed untrusted patterns.
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2026-11-02

# libsqlite3-0 (backend) — FTS5 corrupt-record handling (Debian:
# fix_deferred). podex does not create or query FTS5 tables; unreachable.
CVE-2026-11822 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-11824 exp:2026-11-02

# libudev1 / libsystemd0 — systemd-homed local privilege escalation (Debian:
# fix_deferred). No systemd/homed runs in the containers; unreachable.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-11-02

# util-linux family (util-linux, util-linux-extra, mount, bsdutils, libblkid1,
# libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1) — mount / nsenter / X-mount issues
# (Debian: affected). Require running mount or nsenter with privileges; the
# containers never do. Unreachable.
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-11-02
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-11-02

# openssl / libssl3 (backend) — information disclosure via DTLS handshake
# retransmission (Debian: affected). podex only uses TLS over TCP (HTTPS
# clients, Postgres); DTLS is never used, so the path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-11-02
